  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Preheat the oven to 220C, fan-forced. Line an oven tray with baking paper. Cut the unpeeled potatoes into 2cm-thick wedges. Thinly slice the onion. Coarsely grate the cheese. Drain and rinse the beans.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/840507/photos/large/prep_ingredients-395bd2f9e3cd186ed91c6e8bada328d9.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Roast wedges: Put the potato wedges on the lined tray, drizzle with 1 tbs olive oil, season with salt and pepper and toss to coat. Roast for 20 mins. Scatter over the cheese and roast for a further 5-8 mins until the potato is tender and the cheese is melted.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/840508/photos/large/roast_wedges-28abe9fc16640da7073a6485cf1910f4.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook onion: Meanwhile, heat 2 tsp olive oil in a medium deep frypan over medium heat. Cook the onion, stirring, for 3-4 mins until softened.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/840509/photos/large/cook_onion-3672abcaf59c4c4a789450a05819575c.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Simmer beans: Add the beans, tomatoes, barbecue seasoning, 1 tbs barbecue sauce and ½ tsp sugar to the onion and stir to combine (see Make it spicy). Bring to the boil, then reduce the heat to medium and cook, stirring occasionally, for 5 mins or until slightly thickened. Remove the pan from the heat. Taste, then season with salt and pepper.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/840510/photos/large/add_beans-5e91425fee5aeac82e9165332ca8f9a4.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Combine 2 tsp olive oil and 1 tsp red wine vinegar in a large bowl and season with salt and pepper. Add the salad leaves and toss to coat. Divide the beans, cheesy wedges and salad leaves among bowls. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/840511/photos/large/serve_up-ff287ea82cb882510f5f264ef89384f4.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it spicy: If you like a kick of heat, add a pinch of chilli flakes to the beans, or scatter over to serve if it's just for you.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/840512/photos/large/make_it_spicy-c90b482a7efbd3c11ad2ff7ff044d9af.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
